Theorem RL-26: ownership-event ordering barriers

  Preconditions:
    - A pending logical event refers to value v.
    - The intervening operation is a contract boundary, sharing observation,
      containing-value mutation, or transparent operation.

  Soundness property:
    Event order is preserved across every operation that may observe or change
    v's ownership state. A release remains after v's last use. Physical counter
    motion is permitted only as a projection that refines this order.

  Proof obligation:
    Enumerate three ordering barriers and one transparent case.
    Coverage gate: 4 cases plus release-after-last-use negative witness.

    Engines dispatched:
      rc_counting (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl26_event_ordering_barriers)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)
      case_analysis (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: RL-26 freezes logical ownership-event order across observation boundaries and keeps release after last use
